WEBVTT

0
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:06.660
Sprezzature is an AI engine for Design.
Colors proves your colours can be read.

1
00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.840
Light grey on white reads perfectly well.
At your desk, indoors.

2
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Whoever chose the colour can read it.
That is the whole problem.

3
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.800
Red against green is the other half,
for about 1 man in 12.

4
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.112
Run with no arguments, it audits
the palette this package ships with.

5
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.400
56 pairs a real theme puts together.
22 of them fail.

6
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:47.360
Brand yellow on white is 1.51 to 1,
where plain text needs 4.5.

7
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:51.060
So it exits 1, and the build
that called it stops there.

8
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:56.737
A colour has 3 parts,
and only one of them survives everything.

9
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:03.040
Colour blindness takes the hue.
Grey printing takes the saturation.

10
00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.760
Nothing takes the lightness,
so that is the axis the fix walks.

11
00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:16.480
Along OKLCH, by Björn OTTOSSON,
keeping the nearest colour that passes.

12
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:20.800
The same chart now,
redrawn for each of those eyes.

13
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:27.440
Watch South and East. The hue between
them goes, the bars stay apart.

14
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:32.600
Then no colour at all,
and 3 regions still.

15
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:40.400
The matrices are MACHADO, 2009,
measured on real observers.

16
00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:45.240
Go to sprezzature.ai,
and drop a GitHub star if it deserves it.

17
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:51.920
Make it, audit it, take a look at it.
